content.text:
Now lib files.

routes.ts with absolute URL helpers. site.ts.

Let me write `lib/site.ts` containing config, nav, routes, and helper getLocaleFromPath. Use no React.

```ts
export type Locale = 'fr'|'en';
export const siteUrl = 'https://advensystem.lu';
export const routes = {...} as const;
export const contact = {...};
export const socialLinks = [...]
export const navLabels = {...}
export function homeHref(locale) ...
export function navItems(locale): Array<{label,href}>
```

When building anchor href: `${routes.home[locale]}#about`. With trailingSlash, home fr '/' + '#about' = '/#about'; en '/en/#about'. Good. For portage page, nav About etc to home anchors. For home page, those links will be '/#about' and work. "Accueil" to '/' on home.

Footer nav? no.

For `langSwitch`:
FR home -> /en/
EN home -> /
FR portage -> /en/portage-salarial-luxembourg-2/
EN portage -> /portage-salarial-luxembourg/

We can derive in Header based on pathname: if portage path, switch corresponding; else home.

`isPortagePath(pathname)`.

Content files. Let's write FR/EN home content with types.

Type definitions in `types/index.ts`:
```ts
export type Locale...
```
But lib/site exports Locale. Avoid circular. Put Locale in types. `types/index.ts`:
```ts
export type Locale = "fr" | "en";
export interface NavItem...
export interface Slide...
export interface HomeContent...
export interface PortageContent...
export interface ClientLogo...
```
Import types in content.

Let me define HomeContent:
```ts
interface HomeContent {
 meta: {title, description};
 hero: {title, text, cta};
 slider: {title, cta, slides: {image, alt, caption}[]};
 about: {title, columns: {paragraphs: string[]; image: {src, alt}; imageFirst?: boolean}[]};
 services: {title, intro, items: {title: string[] | string; icon: string}[]}; // title with line breaks maybe array
 why: {title, intro, stats: {value?, suffix?, text}[], cta};
 clients: {title, intro, items: {name, src, width, height}[]};
}
```
For services titles with <br>, use `string[]` lines.
Why cards: `{value?: number, suffix?: string, text: string}`. For non-number, no value.

PortageContent:
```ts
interface PortageStep {label,title,text}
interface PortageContent {
 meta:{title,description}
 hero:{badge,titleLines,text,primaryCta,secondaryCta}
 understanding:{title, paragraphs, stats:{value,label}[], visualTextLines}
 why:{title,intro,cards:{icon:'shield'|'document'|'clock'|'exchange';title,text,tags?:string[]}[]}
 approach:{title,intro,bullets,steps}
 cta:{title,text,boxText,button,note}
}
```
Icons for why cards: original inline svg shield, document, clock, exchange. We'll create an Icon component by name.

Client logos list shared for both locales, alt English? For FR use "Logo SNCF" etc. Alt can be brand names same.

Content: Ensure apostrophes are typographic? Use standard ASCII apostrophes; JSX text handles. For French, use `’` (U+2019) to match? Original uses straight '. Use straight to be consistent, or typographic for polish. Not important. Use typographic apostrophes in display text? I'll use `’` in French text; fine.

Let's write.

