content.text:
Now globals.css. Need body background pattern. Add typography defaults matching original.

```css
@tailwind base;
@tailwind components;
@tailwind utilities;

:root {
  --brand: #003ABD;
}
@layer base {
  html { scroll-behavior: smooth; -webkit-text-size-adjust:100%; }
  body { @apply bg-white text-brand-navy font-sans antialiased; background-image:url('/images/theme/BG.svg'); }
  p, li { ... } // original 25 -> responsive. But Tailwind classes per component better. Global p font-size 18px? original body 25 at >1620, 20 at <=1620, 18 <=950. If we set body font-size 20px, then all unspecified text inherits. Many components set explicit sizes. Let's set body text-[18px] lg:text-[20px]? Can't @apply media easily: `@apply text-[18px] lg:text-[20px];` works. But child p defaults inherit.
  h1..h6 font-normal? Original h1-h3 p margin 0, weight 400. Headings are often styled bold via classes. Set `h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6,p{margin:0}`.
  ::selection ...
  :focus-visible outline...
}
@layer components {
  .site-container { @apply mx-auto w-full max-w-site px-5 sm:px-8 lg:px-10 min-[1621px]:px-0; }
  .content-title { @apply text-center text-[25px] font-bold uppercase leading-tight tracking-[1.5px] text-brand-navy lg:text-[30px]; }
  .section-lead { @apply text-center text-[22px] font-normal leading-[1.35] lg:text-[25px] min-[1621px]:text-[30px]; }
  .btn-gradient {...}
  .btn-outline {...}
}
```
Careful: `max-w-site` needs config; yes.
`min-[1621px]` arbitrary variant works in Tailwind 3.

Buttons: original `.btn` font 25px and padding 17.5 19 23.5. Use `inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-[2px] bg-gradient-to-br from-gold to-coral px-6 pb-5 pt-4 text-[20px] font-normal text-white shadow-card transition hover:shadow-none hover:brightness-105 focus-visible:outline... lg:text-[23px]`. Good.

Add `.text-gradient` for hero title and numbers:
```css
.text-gradient { background: linear-gradient(173.25deg,#003ABD,#00226E); -webkit-background-clip:text; background-clip:text; color:transparent; }
.text-gradient-warm { background: linear-gradient(135deg,#FFC200,#FF785E); ...}
```
Why numbers use warm gradient.

Slider image dark overlay. Use utility.

Add `.section-anchor` scroll-margin-top for anchors: `[id]{scroll-margin-top:120px}` maybe only for #about etc. Since header on home is absolute, anchor scroll doesn't need offset; but portage nav links to home anchors. On home with absolute header, scrolling to #about top is fine (header not sticky). Use scroll-margin-top:20px.

Focus visible: `*:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #FF8C00; outline-offset: 3px; }`.

Form input styles in modal handled by utilities.

Now layout.

`app/layout.tsx`:
```tsx
import type { Metadata, Viewport } from "next";
import { Barlow } from "next/font/google";
import "./globals.css";
import { ContactProvider } from "@/components/contact/ContactProvider";
import { siteUrl } from "@/lib/site";

const barlow = Barlow({...});

export const metadata: Metadata = {
 metadataBase: new URL(siteUrl),
 title: { default:"AdvenSystem", template:"%s – AdvenSystem" },
 description: "...",
 icons: { icon: [{url:"/images/favicon-32x32.png", sizes:"32x32"}, ...], apple:"/images/apple-touch-icon.png" },
 alternates? per page.
 openGraph: { type:'website', siteName:'AdvenSystem', locale:'fr_LU', ...}
 robots: { index:true, follow:true }
};
export const viewport: Viewport = { width:'device-width', initialScale:1, themeColor:'#003ABD' };
```
Note title template + per page title containing "– AdvenSystem" would duplicate. Use absolute titles per page via `title: { absolute: ... }`. We'll do that in page metadata. Or set template and page titles relative. FR home title is long includes AdvenSystem; use absolute. For portage use "Portage Salarial Luxembourg – AdvenSystem" absolute. Good.

Body:
```tsx
<html lang="fr" suppressHydrationWarning>
<body className={`${barlow.variable} font-sans`}>
 <script dangerouslySetInnerHTML.../>
 <ContactProvider>{children}</ContactProvider>
</body>
</html>
```
ContactProvider is client and wraps server children; fine.

Root page group layouts:
app/(fr)/layout.tsx:
```tsx
import { Header } from ...; import { Footer }...
export default function FrLayout({children}) { return <><Header locale="fr"/><main>{children}</main><Footer locale="fr"/></> }
```
Header is absolute; main no padding.

app/(en)/layout.tsx same.

Sitemap and robots. `app/sitemap.ts`:
```ts
import { MetadataRoute } from 'next';
export default function sitemap(): MetadataRoute.Sitemap { const lastModified = new Date(); return [ ... ]; }
```
Use static lastModified? Use new Date() at build; fine. URLs with trailing slash.

robots.ts:
```ts
rules: [{userAgent:'*', allow:'/'}], sitemap: `${siteUrl}/sitemap.xml`, host: siteUrl
```

not-found: `app/not-found.tsx` with its own layout? It renders inside root layout (html/body), but no Header/Footer because it's not inside group layouts. We can include Header locale='fr' and Footer. Header is client. Good. Include links to home FR/EN. metadata title "Page introuvable". Use noindex.

Now components.

Container:
```tsx
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils';
export function Container({className, children}: {className?:string; children:React.ReactNode}) {
 return <div className={cn('mx-auto w-full max-w-site px-5 sm:px-8 lg:px-10 min-[1621px]:px-0', className)}>{children}</div>
}
```

SectionTitle:
```tsx
export function SectionTitle({children, className, as:Tag='h2'}) ...
```
Could just use classes inline. But reuse.

`components/ui/SectionTitle.tsx` with `as` prop; TS complexity. Use simple h2.

`components/ui/Button.tsx`? ContactButton covers modal; external link button maybe. Create `buttonClasses` constant in lib/utils? Let's add:
```ts
export const buttonBase = "...";
```
Then use cn. Add to lib/utils:
`export const btnPrimary = "..."; export const btnGhost = "..."`.
We'll use in components.

Contact components.

ContactProvider:
```tsx
"use client";
import { createContext, useCallback, useContext, useMemo, useState } from "react";
import { usePathname } from "next/navigation";
import { ContactModal } from "./ContactModal";
import { localeFromPath } from "@/lib/site";
type ContactContextValue = { openContact: (source?: string) => void };
const ContactContext = createContext<ContactContextValue | null>(null);
export function useContact() { const ctx=useContext(...); if(!ctx) throw ...; return ctx; }
export function ContactProvider({children}) {
 const [isOpen,setIsOpen]=useState(false);
 const [source,setSource]=useState("AdvenSystem.lu");
 const pathname=usePathname();
 const locale=localeFromPath(pathname ?? "/");
 const openContact=useCallback((src?:string)=>{setSource(src ?? pathname ?? "AdvenSystem.lu");setIsOpen(true);},[pathname]);
 const close=useCallback(()=>setIsOpen(false),[]);
 const value=useMemo(()=>({openContact}),[openContact]);
 return <ContactContext.Provider value={value}>{children}{isOpen&&<ContactModal locale={locale} source={source} onClose={close}/>}</ContactContext.Provider>
}
```
Modal mounted only when open. Good.

ContactButton:
```tsx
"use client";
import { useContact } from ...
export function ContactButton({children, className, source, type='button', ariaLabel}: ...) {
 const {openContact}=useContact();
 return <button type={type} onClick={()=>openContact(source)} className={className} aria-label={ariaLabel}>{children}</button>
}
```
For link-like inline CTAs, button styled.

ContactModal:
- locale texts dictionary.
- fields controlled? Use uncontrolled with FormData from form on submit. Simplest. But need error display. `const formRef`, onSubmit handler reads new FormData(form). Validate client-side using form.checkValidity() (native) and set custom error if polit unchecked (native required handles).
- state: status 'idle'|'submitting'|'success'|'error', message.
- onSubmit:
```ts
e.preventDefault();
if(!form.checkValidity()){ form.reportValidity(); return; }
const fd = new FormData(form);
const payload = Object.fromEntries...
payload.polit = fd.get('polit')==='on' or 'yes';
setStatus('submitting');
const res = await fetch('/api/contact',{method:'POST',headers...,body:JSON.stringify(payload)});
const data = await res.json().catch(()=>null);
if(res.ok && data?.ok){setStatus('success'); form.reset();}
else { setStatus('error'); setMessage(mapError(data?.code)); }
```
- On 503 code 'not_configured', message: "Le formulaire n’est pas encore configuré sur ce serveur. Merci d’écrire à contact@advensystem.lu ou d’appeler le +352 661 11 22 60." EN analog. For other errors: "L’envoi a échoué. Merci de réessayer..." 
- Success screen matches original wording; only after actual success.
- Close buttons: x icon (use delete_sign_filled.svg image) and backdrop.
- Focus trap: keydown Tab cycle within dialog; Escape.
- aria-labelledby.
- Body overflow hidden.
- Use a `useEffect` on mount to focus first input, store active element, restore on unmount.
- Overlay uses fixed inset-0 with backdrop-blur-[3px]; background rgba(0,34,110,0.7) on backdrop.
- Dialog width 420px max-w-[calc(100vw-2rem)], bg white with bg-form.svg cover.
- Form paddings 33/60/50.
- Inputs underline style: `w-full border-0 border-b border-brand bg-transparent px-0 pt-3 pb-1 text-sm text-brand placeholder:text-brand focus:border-b-2 focus:border-[#ffb100] focus:ring-0 outline-none`. Tailwind focus:border-b-2 may shift. Fine.
- Textarea border full, h-30.
- Checkbox: use native with `accent-brand` and text 12px.
- Submit button full? Original width 170px centered; mobile 100%. Use `mx-auto block w-[170px] max-sm:w-full`.
- Error banner.

Icons: We can inline an SVG close; but original uses delete_sign_filled.svg. Use Image? Use img 19px. Good.

Header uses images. Let's write Contact components and Header/Footer.

Header details:

```tsx
"use client";
import Image from "next/image";
import Link from "next/link";
import { usePathname } from "next/navigation";
import { useEffect, useState } from "react";
import { company, languageHref, localeFromPath, navItems, routes } from "@/lib/site";
