```
Path normalization:
```ts
const pathname = usePathname() ?? "/";
const locale = props.locale;
const home = routes.home[locale];
const normalized = pathname.replace(/\/+$/, "") || "/";
const homeNorm = home.replace(/\/+$/, "") || "/";
const isHome = normalized === homeNorm;
const isPage = !isHome;
const isPortage = ...
```
Nav current: link href route. For "Accueil" current if isHome. "Portage Salarial" current if isPortage. For hash links, no current.

Header class:
```tsx
<header className={cn("absolute inset-x-0 top-0 z-40", isPage ? "bg-white shadow-[0_2px_16px_rgba(0,0,0,0.10)] pt-[30px] pb-[24px] lg:pt-[38px]" : "pt-8 lg:pt-[74px]")}>
```
Wait home nav dark text; logo. page header white.

Container flex:
- Logo Link with `aria-label="AdvenSystem – Accueil"`, Image width 278 height 52, class `h-auto w-[210px] lg:w-[240px] xl:w-[278px]`, priority.
- Desktop nav hidden below 1150: `hidden min-[1151px]:flex flex-1 items-center justify-end gap-6 xl:gap-8`.
  - `<nav aria-label={locale==='fr'?'Navigation principale':'Main navigation'}><ul className="flex items-center gap-4 xl:gap-[22px]">{...}</ul></nav>`
  - right block: `<div className="flex items-start gap-4 xl:gap-5">`
    - phone: `<a href=... className="group flex flex-col items-center"> <span className="flex items-center gap-2 text-[20px]..."><img src phone-orange class=20 />{phone}</span><span className="text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[1px] opacity-40">{label}</span></a>`
    Actually original phone number is on top, label below. Add icon in pseudo before. Use phone icon 20px.
    - language: `<div className="flex items-center gap-2">` links 30px circles border-2 border-accent text accent for inactive; active gradient text-white border-transparent.
    - socials: vertical `flex flex-col gap-3` 30px icons.
  - The nav + phone may overflow at 1151. Original had small. We can reduce font sizes at xl. Use `text-[16px] xl:text-[18px]` and hide socials below 1300? Keep but gap smaller. At 1151–1300, 7 nav items at 16px plus phone etc may overflow. Let's calculate: nav labels total ~500px + gaps 6*12=72 => 572; phone 150; lang 70; social 30; logo 278; gaps ~100 => 1200. At 1151 tight. Hide socials below 1280 (`hidden min-[1280px]:flex`) and phone label maybe. Use `max-[1280px]:hidden` for socials. Fine.
- Mobile controls `min-[1151px]:hidden flex items-center gap-3`: phone icon link (visible), hamburger button.
- Hamburger button: `inline-flex h-[45px] w-[45px] items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-brand` with 3 spans. Use aria-expanded. Animate to X with classes maybe.
- Mobile panel: `min-[1151px]:hidden` conditional, `<div id="mobile-menu" className="absolute inset-x-0 top-full bg-brand py-5 shadow-lg">` with nav list and contact info. Since header is absolute, top-full works. Links white 18 centered py-4. Include language & socials row, phone.
  - Use `open` state; close on pathname change (useEffect).
  - Also close when clicking hash links (onClick close). Good.
- On page variant, header white; mobile panel blue.

Potential z-index: header z-40, modal z-[100].

Home intro pt must account for header; yes.

Footer:
```tsx
import Image from 'next/image'; import { company, routes }...
export function Footer({locale}) {
 const t = {...}
 return <footer id="contacts" className="bg-brand bg-[url('/images/theme/BG_footer.svg')] bg-cover bg-center text-white shadow-panel">
